   "summary": "The study measured the foraging strategies (solitary vs. group) and associated behaviors (diaspore removal time and discovery time) of nine different ant species. The measurements covered multiple species to compare how ant size and foraging strategy relate to their efficiency in removing artificial diaspores. The study measured the efficiency of diaspore removal by solitary versus group-foraging ants, finding that solitary foragers removed more diaspores, and also examined how nest distance affected diaspore removal."
